#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# THE SESSION'S TICK. Detach this and the page has a frame edge.
#
#     detach RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs view=<Surface>
#
# ONE LOOP, on the thread this `detach` asked for -- not a stream pair. The
# pacing is a number on the Presentable family and presenting is a step on it
# (ontology/PresentableBase.h, on why a standing produce body gives a pool a
# minimum size), so there is no ring, no producer and no pool occupant.
#
# IT DRIVES MORE THAN THIS SURFACE. RunFrames advances every entity that claims
# Animated (ontology/Animated.h), so the toolbar's click-and-hold repeat and the
# layer window's isolation fade ride this same tick. A session needs exactly one
# caller of it; a session with no surface at all can drive the family from its
# own loop instead.
#
# The argument in the other direction still holds: Vulkan is happy to submit and
# present from a thread that did not create the window, GLFW is not happy to be
# polled from one that did not. Nothing here touches PollEvents.

requires view [Surface, Presentable]

# The argument is the pacing in ms. Zero means unpaced -- present on every visit
# and let this loop's rate set the frame rate, which is the honest way to ask how
# fast the pipeline can actually go.
view.RunFrames(16)
